{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Alpine Loop Automation Failure During Storm",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The zone 1 impedance setting of the protection relay was 6.0 ohms, while the actual line impedance was 12.5 ohms.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The automation logic lacked a directional check for distinguishing a reverse fault from a forward fault.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The tie switch closing did not examine the source side potential to confirm a permanent clearance.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The storm mode flag was disabled, and the feeder protection used a standard two-shot reclosing count.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A lightning bolt struck the Synthetic Alpine feeder conductor at 14:23, creating a phase-to-ground fault.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A second lightning stroke at 14:25 initiated a phase-to-phase fault on the same feeder.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A tree branch blown by winds at 14:31 contacted a bare phase conductor, causing a high-impedance fault.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "An internal flashover in the loop sectionalizer's insulated switch produced a second phase-to-ground fault at 14:33.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Because of the incorrect setting, the relay erroneously localized the phase-to-ground fault to the distant line section.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The erroneous localization produced a trip signal that opened the healthy loop tie sectionalizer, not the faulty one.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the tie sectionalizer opened, the loss-of-voltage detection prompted a close command to the normally open tie switch.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The tie switch closed onto the still-faulted line, causing a severe overcurrent that tripped the upstream breaker.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "Approximately 300 customers were without power for 210 minutes after the healthy lateral was misisolated.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The repeated overcurrents shortened the life of the main line cable by an estimated 4.5 years.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 5, 6, 7, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "A voltage swell caused by the tie switch closing damaged a surge suppressor at a factory on the feeder.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The misoperation was not caused by the lightning surges but by the missing directional and permissive logic.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1, 2]
        },
        {
          "text": "Protection engineers calibrated the relay distance zone to match the actual 12.5-ohm loop impedance.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The automation firmware was upgraded to include a directional angle blocking element for fault isolation.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "Crews installed a potential-sensing permissive on the tie switch to require a live source before closing.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The protection team reprogrammed the recloser to require storm-mode enable and a one-shot process during storms.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Creek and Synthetic Lake Loop Restoration Failure in Snowstorm",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The Ethernet link between Synthetic Creek and Synthetic Lake had a latency of 800 ms, exceeding the automation's 100 ms limit.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The loop restoration logic did not have a voltage check before closing the tie switch.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The fault current pickup in the sectionalizer was set to 600 A, but the minimum fault level was 850 A.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "An error in the test procedure had disabled the supervisory alarm that might have indicated the active setting mismatch.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 15:12, snow accretion caused a conductor sag and a phase-to-phase contact on Synthetic Feeder 9.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A lightning storm later caused an insulator flashover at Synthetic Creek, creating a second ground fault.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A remote end substation's switchgear operation sent a false voltage signal to the loop controller.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The back-up battery at the controller expired, eliminating the last source of clean status information.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "If the link latency exceeds 100 ms, the controller falsely interprets the feeder as lost and issues a sectionalizer open command.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The healthy sectionalizer opened, isolating a large commercial load but allowing a reverse power flow to a distributed generator.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The controller then commanded the tie switch to close to restore the interrupted commercial area.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [1, 7, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The tie switch closed while the two sources were out of phase, resulting in a large circulating current.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "A total of 1,200 customers lost service for 2.5 hours due to the open sectionalizer and the tie close shock.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The circulating current caused thermal damage to the bus bar and a subsequent transformer overcurrent.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "The commercial facility's solid-state breaker tripped immediately, interrupting a continuous chemical process for the full 150-minute outage.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The event was not caused by the snowstorm's ice but by the communication and control logic defects.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineers reduced the communication latency by installing fiber optic links instead of the old copper network.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The loop restoration software was updated to include a voltage synchronism check before any tie switch close.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sectionalizer pickup was adjusted down to 500 A, ensuring detection of all winter low-level faults.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "A weekly verification procedure was introduced to ensure the supervisory alarms and settings remain active.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
